## Reading the A15 result

Everything lands in the ram console (read as `/proc/last_kmsg` from TWRP).
Look for, in order:

1. `NUXEL_MARKER INITRAMFS_EXECUTED`, then the new `FIRSTLIGHT …` block:
   `NUXEL_FB_INFO` + one `=value` line per geometry field, then
   `NUXEL_FB_BUFFERS_PAINTED=2`, `NUXEL_FB_ANIM frame=1..11`,
   `NUXEL_FB_ANIM_DONE frames=12`, `NUXEL_FB_DRAW_SUCCESS`,
   `NUXEL_MARKER FIRSTLIGHT_ANIMATION_DONE` and
   `NUXEL_MARKER FIRSTLIGHT_FRAME_WRITTEN`. **Record the geometry lines
   verbatim** — they are the only hardware description of the fbdev we have
   (compare `smem_start`/`smem_len` with the DECON's 35,020,800-byte window[5]).
2. `NUXEL_MARKER ROOTFS_MOUNTED`, the syscall/spawn probe tables,
   `NUXEL_MARKER FEDORA_BINARY_EXECUTED`, `NUXEL_MARKER SYSTEMD_PATCH_PRESENT`.
3. **`NUXEL_MARKER CGROUP2_MOUNTED`** (or `CGROUP2_MOUNT_FAILED`).
4. `NUXEL_MARKER ROOTFS_HANDOFF_STARTED`, then `systemd[1]:` lines.
5. **The absence of any reboot request.** The decisive test: does the log reach
   t ≥ 60 s with no `debug-snapshot: normal reboot starting`? A14's appeared at
   t=47.171 s. If A15 shows a reboot at ~47 s again, the watchdog was not the
   (only) cause and the next hypothesis is the kernel-side vendor watchdog path.
6. Whether the `Failed at step CGROUP` / `Failed to attach to cgroup` messages
   are gone. If they are gone and units now execute, milestone 16 is met; if they
   are replaced by a *different* unit failure, read the exact errno and unit
   before changing anything.

Interpretation rules
* `FIRSTLIGHT_FRAME_WRITTEN` without an operator-visible image is a **display
  driver** result, not a process-execution result. It has already been achieved
  once (A14) and may not be claimed twice as progress.
* If the phone returns to TWRP: record
  `BOOT_RESULT=FAILED_USER_RETURNED_TO_TWRP`, capture `last_kmsg` + pstore into
  `scripts/s10plus-debug-pack/captures/<stamp>-A15-postfail/`, compare with A14
  and continue. Do not re-run an identical candidate.
* If the frame *is* visible: the next two steps are (a) hold the frame steady and
  (b) start Phoc/Phosh investigation, which needs DRM/KMS (5.4+ Exynos 9820 port)
  and therefore does not belong in the same cycle as a display fix.

## Reproducing this cycle's pipeline (all committed and gated)

```
# 0. kernel tree MUST be a fresh extraction: /b/src and /b/src2 in the podman
#    container are silently truncated (scripts/Kbuild.include was 0 bytes).
sh .scratch/kb.sh sh -c 'rm -rf /b/k15 && mkdir -p /b/k15 && \
  tar xzf /b/kernel.tar.gz -C /b/k15 --strip-components=1'
podman cp boot/initramfs/init.sh      nuxel-kb:/b/a15/initramfs-src-init.sh   # reference
# 1. initramfs (macOS side, proven newc.py edits, fails loudly on a missing anchor)
sed -e 's|/A14$|/A15|' .scratch/s10plus-cycle4/a13/build-a14-initramfs.sh \
  > .scratch/s10plus-cycle4/a13/build-a15-initramfs.sh
sh .scratch/s10plus-cycle4/a13/build-a15-initramfs.sh
# 2. first-light payload (container compiles aarch64 natively)
podman cp tools/s10plus/nuxel-fb-phone.c nuxel-kb:/b/a15/nuxel-fb-phone.c
sh .scratch/kb.sh sh -c 'cd /b/a15 && gcc -O2 -static -nostdlib -ffreestanding \
  -fno-stack-protector -fno-builtin -Wl,-e,_start -o nuxel-fb-phone-aarch64 \
  nuxel-fb-phone.c'
podman cp nuxel-kb:/b/a15/nuxel-fb-phone-aarch64 tools/s10plus/nuxel-fb-phone-aarch64
# 3. kernel with the initramfs embedded (container)
podman cp build/out/s10plus/debug-candidates/A15/initramfs.cpio nuxel-kb:/b/a15/initramfs.cpio
podman cp .scratch/s10plus-cycle4/a13/relax-werror.sh  nuxel-kb:/b/a15/relax-werror.sh
podman cp .scratch/s10plus-cycle4/a13/build-a15-kernel2.sh nuxel-kb:/b/a15/kbuild.sh
sh .scratch/kb.sh sh -c 'sh /b/a15/kbuild.sh'
# 4. boot container + gates
boot/s10plus/build-candidate.sh --kernel <Image-A15> --initramfs-cpio <A15 cpio> \
  --init none --no-dev-nodes --compress lzma --out build/out/s10plus/debug-candidates/A15/boot.img
sh boot/s10plus/tests/test-boot-image-gates.sh
sh boot/s10plus/tests/test-init-cmdline-independence.sh
```

Rules that held for this cycle: `podman machine start` is never used (the gvproxy
socket path resets the VM and truncates files mid-copy); writes into the
container go through `podman cp` (stdin piping silently produces 0-byte files);
every artifact copied out is hash-verified.

## Standing risks
* No real stock BOOT backup exists. RECOVERY untouched; every write BOOT-only.
* A12 is the regression baseline and is never overwritten.
